      "id": "y4rtjsf",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Meaning of Motion"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Distance is the total scalar path length covered, while displacement is the shortest vector distance between initial and final points.",
        "Speed measures the rate of distance covered, whereas velocity measures displacement over time with direction.",
        "Acceleration measures the rate of change of velocity over time.",
        "The three standard equations of motion describe relationships between initial velocity, final velocity, acceleration, time, and displacement.",
        "Graphs of motion provide visual representations where slope and area under curves yield speed, velocity, and displacement."
      ],
      "id": "z188sx2"
    },
